<div class="rich-text w-full"><p>India’s logistics market was valued at USD 228.4 billion in 2024 and is projected to reach USD 428.7 billion by 2033, growing at around 6.5% a year. Yet the industry still faces persistent and costly challenges.</p></div>
<div class="rich-text w-full"><h2>Five problems holding logistics back</h2></div>
<div class="rich-text w-full"><ul><li><strong>Inefficient fleet management:</strong> over 35% of trucks in India run empty, causing $5 billion in annual losses.</li><li><strong>Manual warehousing:</strong> 80% of Indian warehouses lack automation, leading to inventory losses and reduced throughput.</li><li><strong>No real-time route optimization:</strong> traffic delays cost Indian logistics over ₹1.47 trillion annually.</li><li><strong>Limited visibility:</strong> fragmented systems lower supply chain transparency and hamper decision-making and accountability.</li><li><strong>Driver fatigue and safety risks:</strong> 25% of road accidents in India are linked to commercial vehicle driver fatigue.</li></ul></div>
<div class="rich-text w-full"><h2>An integrated answer</h2></div>
<div class="rich-text w-full"><p>NeuroSky tackles these inefficiencies with an integrated, AI-powered logistics ecosystem: AI-driven fleet management, driver behavior monitoring, smart warehouse automation, and drone-assisted navigation, all tied together by unified dashboards that deliver transparency, compliance, and strategic insight.</p></div>
<div class="rich-text w-full"><p>The global logistics market is expected to grow from USD 3,797 billion in 2024 to around USD 7,754 billion by 2034. The businesses that modernize now will be the ones that lead it.</p></div>
